o, Pro+, and Max tiers, allowing AI-assisted debugging of workflow failures.\",\n    71→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    72→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n    73→    \"date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n    74→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    75→  },\n    76→  {\n    77→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n    78→    \"title\": \"Visual Studio and VS Code May/June Updates\",\n    79→    \"description\": \"GitHub released Copilot updates for Visual Studio (May update) and Visual Studio Code with Copilot Chat bringing richer context to pull requests.\",\n    80→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    81→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n    82→    \"date\": \"2026-06-03\",\n    83→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    84→  },\n    85→  {\n    86→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    87→    \"title\": \"Design Mode Improvements with Multi-Select and Voice Input\",\n    88→    \"description\": \"Cursor enhanced Design Mode with multi-select elements, voice input capabilities, and improved component styling. Users can now click multiple elements simultaneously, narrate changes by voice, and queue new instructions while agents are running.\",\n    89→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    90→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    91→    \"date\": \"2026-06-03\",\n    92→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    93→  },\n    94→  {\n    95→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    96→    \"title\": \"SDK Updates: Custom Tools, Auto-Review, and Nested Subagents\",\n    97→    \"description\": \"Cursor SDK now supports custom tools, auto-review routing for safer headless execution, JSONL and custom stores for persistence, and nested subagents. Both TypeScript and Python SDKs received reliability and performance improvements.\",\n    98→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    99→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   100→    \"date\": \"2026-06-03\",\n   101→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   102→  },\n   103→  {\n   104→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   105→    \"title\": \"June 2026 Release Wave - Copilot Enhancements\",\n   106→    \"description\": \"GitHub released multiple Copilot updates in early June 2026, including larger context windows with configurable reasoning levels, Copilot Chat improvements for pull requests, and the general availability of Enterprise Teams. Additional updates include agent tasks REST API for Copilot Pro tiers, budget and usage management APIs, and billing usage reports API.\",\n   107→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   108→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n   109→    \"date\": \"2026-06-02\",\n   110→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   111→      {\n   112→        \"quote\": \"As per the tool my usage as per April 2026 usage will cost me USD$519.26. This is pretty expensive and not at all affordable.\",\n   113→        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n   114→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   115→      },\n   116→      {\n   117→        \"quote\": \"End of an Era - GitHub Copilot is moving to usage-based billing on June 1, 2026.\",\n   118→        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n   119→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   120→      }\n   121→    ]\n   122→  },\n   123→  {\n   124→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   125→    \"title\": \"Copilot SDK Generally Available\",\n   126→    \"description\": \"The Copilot SDK became generally available in June 2026, providing developers with programmatic access to Copilot capabilities.\",\n   127→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   128→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/\",\n   129→    \"date\": \"2026-06-02\",\n   130→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   131→  },\n   132→  {\n   133→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   134→    \"title\": \"Sites Preview - Build and Deploy Websites\",\n   135→    \"description\": \"Sites is now available in preview in the Codex app. Users can create, save, deploy, and inspect websites, dashboards, internal tools, web apps, and games hosted by OpenAI. Included in ChatGPT Business workspaces and available to ChatGPT Enterprise via RBAC.\",\n   136→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   137→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\",\n   138→    \"date\": \"2026-06-02\",\n   139→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   140→      {\n   141→        \"quote\": \"Two Codex updates landed June 2, 2026: Sites preview in the Codex app - Codex can now create, save, deploy, and inspect websites, dashboards.\",\n   142→        \"source\": \"Reddit\",\n   143→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n   144→      }\n   145→    ]\n   146→  },\n   147→  {\n   148→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   149→    \"title\": \"iOS App Updates - Face ID Lock and Windows SSH Support\",\n   150→    \"description\": \"ChatGPT for iOS 1.2026.146 added optional Face ID/passcode lock for Codex, new settings screen for Queue/Steer behavior, and support for connecting to Windows machines over SSH.\",\n   151→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   152→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\",\n   153→    \"date\": \"2026-06-02\",\n   154→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   155→  },\n   156→  {\n   157→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n   158→    \"title\": \"Claude Opus 4.8 Released\",\n   159→    \"description\": \"Claude Opus 4.8 was released as the new default model for Max/Team plans, showing improvements over Opus 4.7 in coding with notable security enhancements.\",\n   160→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   161→    \"url\": \"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\",\n   162→    \"date\": \"2026-06-02\",\n   163→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   164→      {\n   165→        \"quote\": \"Lots of people want to try Claude Opus 4.8\",\n   166→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   167→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n   168→      },\n   169→      {\n   170→        \"quote\": \"Discussion about Claude Code potentially being called Opus, with a note about CLI stopping working from June 18, 2026\",\n   171→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   172→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n   173→      }\n   174→    ]\n   175→  },\n   176→  {\n   177→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   178→    \"title\": \"Amazon Bedrock Model Provider Support\",\n   179→    \"description\": \"Codex can now use supported OpenAI models available through Amazon Bedrock. Configure Amazon Bedrock as the model provider to run Codex locally with AWS-managed authentication, account controls, and billing.\",\n   180→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   181→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\",\n   182→    \"date\": \"2026-06-01\",\n   183→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   184→  },\n   185→  {\n   186→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   187→    \"title\": \"Terminal Placement Controls\",\n   188→    \"description\": \"Codex app 26.601 added Default terminal location setting. When bottom panel is enabled, users can choose whether terminal shortcuts open in bottom panel or right panel.\",\n   189→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   190→    \"url\": \"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\",\n   191→    \"date\": \"2026-06-01\",\n   192→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   193→  },\n   194→  {\n   195→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n   196→    \"title\": \"Week 22 Updates - v2.1.150 to v2.1.157\",\n   197→    \"description\": \"Multiple releases during May 25-29, 2026 including improvements to rendering performance for large file writes (v2.1.169 mentioned), and ongoing iterative updates to the Claude Code tooling.\",\n   198→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   199→    \"url\": \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\",\n   200→    \"date\": \"2026-05-29\",\n   201→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   202→  }\n   203→]\n   204→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
