s=\"item-meta\">\n   323→                        <span class=\"tag\">agent tools</span>\n   324→                        <span class=\"tag\">APIs</span>\n   325→                        <span class=\"tag\">infrastructure</span>\n   326→                    </div>\n   327→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 27, 2026</div>\n   328→                </div>\n   329→\n   330→                <div class=\"item\">\n   331→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   332→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/tabstack\" target=\"_blank\">Tabstack Web Research</a>\n   333→                    </div>\n   334→                    <div class=\"item-description\">API service that runs autonomous research agents with cited answers in a single API call, enabling web data extraction and browser automation without scrapers.</div>\n   335→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   336→                        <span class=\"tag\">research agent</span>\n   337→                        <span class=\"tag\">API</span>\n   338→                        <span class=\"tag\">automation</span>\n   339→                    </div>\n   340→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • Jun 1, 2026</div>\n   341→                </div>\n   342→\n   343→                <div class=\"item\">\n   344→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   345→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/mistral-vibe\" target=\"_blank\">Mistral Vibe</a>\n   346→                    </div>\n   347→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI agent designed for long-running, multi-step work and coding tasks, built by Mistral AI as part of their agent tooling ecosystem for autonomous development workflows.</div>\n   348→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   349→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   350→                        <span class=\"tag\">Mistral AI</span>\n   351→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow</span>\n   352→                    </div>\n   353→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • Jun 1, 2026</div>\n   354→                </div>\n   355→\n   356→                <div class=\"item\">\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   358→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/calling-skills-for-ai-agents\" target=\"_blank\">Calling Skills for AI Agents</a>\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Developer tool that enables AI agents and coding assistants to add voice and video calling capabilities via GitHub integration.</div>\n   361→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   362→                        <span class=\"tag\">communication</span>\n   363→                        <span class=\"tag\">GitHub</span>\n   364→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow</span>\n   365→                    </div>\n   366→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 27, 2026</div>\n   367→                </div>\n   368→\n   369→                <div class=\"item\">\n   370→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   371→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/phasr\" target=\"_blank\">Phasr</a>\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source productivity tool that enables running 100+ workflows simultaneously without losing context, designed for AI-powered task management.</div>\n   374→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   375→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow</span>\n   376→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   377→                        <span class=\"tag\">productivity</span>\n   378→                    </div>\n   379→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 27, 2026</div>\n   380→                </div>\n   381→\n   382→                <div class=\"item\">\n   383→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   384→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/vibedock\" target=\"_blank\">Vibedock</a>\n   385→                    </div>\n   386→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Mac menu bar utility that lets developers toggle Claude Code MCP servers on and off with one click, streamlining Claude Code ecosystem management.</div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   388→                        <span class=\"tag\">IDE integration</span>\n   389→                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   390→                        <span class=\"tag\">macOS</span>\n   391→                    </div>\n   392→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 23, 2026</div>\n   393→                </div>\n   394→\n   395→                <div class=\"item\">\n   396→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   397→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/command-a\" target=\"_blank\">Command A+</a>\n   398→                    </div>\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Cohere's open-source enterprise workhorse model released under Apache 2.0 license as a 218B sparse model for enterprise AI applications.</div>\n   400→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   401→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   402→                        <span class=\"tag\">model</span>\n   403→                        <span class=\"tag\">Cohere</span>\n   404→                    </div>\n   405→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 23, 2026</div>\n   406→                </div>\n   407→\n   408→                <div class=\"item\">\n   409→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   410→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/forsy\" target=\"_blank\">Forsy</a>\n   411→                    </div>\n   412→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Platform that enables users to capture and monetize their AI agent workflow data, part of the growing ecosystem around AI agents and their operational data.</div>\n   413→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   414→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow</span>\n   415→                        <span class=\"tag\">data</span>\n   416→                        <span class=\"tag\">monetization</span>\n   417→                    </div>\n   418→                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 23, 2026</div>\n   419→                </div>\n   420→            </section>\n   421→\n   422→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   423→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates section\">\n   424→                <div class=\"section-header\">Product Updates</div>\n   425→\n   426→                <div class=\"item\">\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   428→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot SDK GA</a>\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-description\">The Copilot SDK became generally available, providing developers with programmatic access to Copilot capabilities.</div>\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   432→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   433→                        <span class=\"tag\">SDK</span>\n   434→                    </div>\n   435→                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 2, 2026</div>\n   436→                </div>\n   437→\n   438→                <div class=\"item\">\n   439→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   440→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">June 2026 Copilot Wave</a>\n   441→                    </div>\n   442→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Multiple Copilot updates including larger context windows with configurable reasoning levels, Chat improvements for PRs, and Enterprise Teams GA.</div>\n   443→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   444→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   445→                        <span class=\"tag\">context</span>\n   446→                        <span class=\"tag\">enterprise</span>\n   447→                    </div>\n   448→                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 2, 2026</div>\n   449→                </div>\n   450→\n   451→                <div class=\"item\">\n   452→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   453→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">GPT-5.2 Models Deprecated</a>\n   454→                    </div>\n   455→                    <div class=\"item-description\">GitHub deprecated GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex models for Copilot users as part of the June 2026 update cycle.</div>\n   456→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   457→                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Deprecated</span>\n   458→                        <span class=\"tag\">models</span>\n   459→                    </div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 5, 2026</div>\n   461→                </div>\n   462→\n   463→                <div class=\"item\">\n   464→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   465→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Fix with Copilot for Actions</a>\n   466→                    </div>\n   467→                    <div class=\"item-description\">New 'Fix with Copilot' feature for failing GitHub Actions available in Pro, Pro+, and Max tiers for AI-assisted debugging.</div>\n   468→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   469→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   470→                        <span class=\"tag\">debugging</span>\n   471→                        <span class=\"tag\">CI/CD</span>\n   472→                    </div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 4, 2026</div>\n   474→                </div>\n   475→\n   476→                <div class=\"item\">\n   477→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   478→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">VS IDE Updates May/June</a>\n   479→                    </div>\n   480→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Copilot updates for Visual Studio (May) and VS Code with Copilot Chat bringing richer context to pull requests.</div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   482→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   483→                        <span class=\"tag\">VS Code</span>\n   484→                        <span class=\"tag\">PRs</span>\n   485→                    </div>\n   486→                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 3, 2026</div>\n   487→                </div>\n   488→            </section>\n   489→\n   490→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   491→            <section class=\"technical-insights section\">\n   492→                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   493→\n   494→                <div class=\"item\">\n   495→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   496→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/08/microsofts-open-source-tools-were-hacked-to-steal-passwords-of-ai-developers/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Tools Hacked</a>\n   497→                    </div>\n   498→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Microsoft shut down dozens of GitHub code repositories for Azure and AI coding tools after a security breach that stole AI developers' passwords.</div>\n   499→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   500→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   501→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   502→                    </div>\n   503→                    <div class=\"source\">TechCrunch • Jun 8, 2026</div>\n   504→                </div>\n   505→\n   506→                <div class=\"item\">\n   507→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   508→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/openai-help-lockdown-mode/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Lockdown Mode</a>\n   509→                    </div>\n   510→                    <div class=\"item-description\">OpenAI released Lockdown Mode to help prevent data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests.</div>\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   512→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   513→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   514→                        <span class=\"tag\">prompt injection</span>\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"source\">Simon Willison • Jun 5, 2026</div>\n   517→                </div>\n   518→\n   519→                <div class=\"item\">\n   520→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   521→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/ladybird-no-public-prs/\" target=\"_blank\">Ladybird No Public PRs</a>\n   522→                    </div>\n   523→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Ladybird browser will no longer accept public PRs because AI-generated patches no longer indicate substantial effort or good faith.</div>\n   524→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   525→                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   526→                        <span class=\"tag\">open source</span>\n   527→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI ethics</span>\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                    <div class=\"source\">Simon Willison • Jun 5, 2026</div>\n   530→                </div>\n   531→\n   532→                <div class=\"item\">\n   533→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   534→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/ai-enthusiists-race-against-time/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Enthusiasts vs Skeptics</a>\n   535→                    </div>\n   536→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Charity Majors captures the dynamic: enthusiasts see discontinuous leaps and can't afford to wait, while skeptics see reliability degrade with no natural feedback loop connecting them.</div>\n   537→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   538→                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   539→                        <span class=\"tag\">engineering culture</span>\n   540→                    </div>\n   541→                    <div class=\"source\">Simon Willison • Jun 4, 2026</div>\n   542→                </div>\n   543→\n   544→                <div class=\"item\">\n   545→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   546→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/3/uber-caps-ai-tools/\" target=\"_blank\">Uber Caps AI Tool Costs</a>\n   547→                    </div>\n   548→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Uber limiting all employees to $1,500 monthly token spending per AI coding tool after reportedly blowing their 2026 AI budget in four months.</div>\n   549→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   550→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   551→                        <span class=\"tag\">cost management</span>\n   552→                        <span class=\"tag\">enterprise</span>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→                    <div class=\"source\">Simon Willison • Jun 3, 2026</div>\n   555→                </div>\n   556→            </section>\n   557→        </main>\n   558→    </div>\n   559→\n   560→    <footer>\n   561→        <div class=\"container\">\n   562→            <p>Agentic Coding Research Report • Generated on June 10, 2026 • <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> • <a href=\"#\">About</a></p>\n   563→        </div>\n   564→    </footer>\n   565→</body>\n   566→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
