ools, APIs and services without requiring individual API keys or account configurations, unblocking agents to discover and use services autonomously.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"product-tag\">AI developer infrastructure</span>\n                        <span>Released: 2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"Like OpenRouter for agent tools\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Product Hunt</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"product-item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/mistral-vibe\" target=\"_blank\">Mistral Vibe</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-description\">\n                        AI agent designed for long-running, multi-step work and coding tasks, built by Mistral AI as part of their agent tooling ecosystem for autonomous development workflows.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"product-tag\">code agent</span>\n                        <span>Released: 2026-06-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"Agent for long-running, multi-step work and coding\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Product Hunt</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"product-item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/tabstack\" target=\"_blank\">Tabstack Web Research</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-description\">\n                        API service that runs autonomous research agents with cited answers in a single API call, enabling web data extraction and browser automation without scrapers. Works with 50M+ brands in one API call for developer workflows.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"product-tag\">research agent</span>\n                        <span>Released: 2026-06-01</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"Run a research agent with cited answers in a single API call\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Product Hunt</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"product-item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">\n                        <a href=\"https://powabase.com\" target=\"_blank\">Powabase</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-description\">\n                        Backend-as-a-service platform for AI-native applications combining PostgreSQL, RAG, AI agents, memory management, workflows, and automation primitives in a single PostgreSQL-native stack, solving the complexity of building AI apps with tightly coupled vector storage.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"product-tag\">AI coding platform</span>\n                        <span>Released: 2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"#1 Product on May 27, 2026\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Product Hunt</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"product-item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/phasr\" target=\"_blank\">Phasr</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-description\">\n                        Open-source productivity tool that enables running 100+ workflows simultaneously without losing context, designed for AI-powered task management and workflow orchestration.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"product-tag\">workflow automation</span>\n                        <span>Released: 2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"Run 100+ workflows simultaneously without losing context\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Product Hunt</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"product-item\">\n                    <div class=\"product-name\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/calling-skills-for-ai-agents\" target=\"_blank\">Calling Skills for AI Agents</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-description\">\n                        Developer tool that enables AI agents and coding assistants to add voice and video calling capabilities via GitHub integration, expanding the communication modalities available to AI development tools.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"product-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"product-tag\">AI coding workflow tool</span>\n                        <span>Released: 2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"Add voice and video calling via your coding agent\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Product Hunt</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Product Updates (19)</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Codex CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT for iOS Updates - June 9, 2026</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">Release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Codex iOS app 1.2026.153 added support for choosing branches, creating worktrees, running environment setup scripts, new Codex profile screen with usage stats, /goal support for mobile, inline review comments, and side chat from selected transcript text.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-09</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Canvas Design Mode and Context Usage Report</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Design Mode is now available in canvases for faster editing. Cursor can also display context usage as an interactive canvas report, breaking down token usage across system prompts, tools, rules, and skills.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-05</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Organizations for Cursor Enterprise</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Enterprise customers can now manage multiple Cursor teams from one organization with separate security, governance, budget, and feature controls. Includes organizations, teams, and groups hierarchy with granular permissions.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-05</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Auto-Review Run Mode</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        New Auto-Review run mode allows Cursor to work longer with fewer approval prompts. A classifier subagent decides which tool calls run automatically, which to sandbox, and which to require human approval. Configurable via Settings and permissions.json.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-05</div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"Auto mode is now usage-based (already hit $7)\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Reddit (negative sentiment)</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex Models Deprecated</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-announcement\">Announcement</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        GitHub deprecated GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex models for Copilot users as part of the June 2026 update cycle.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-05</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Codex CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Activity Insights and Share Cards</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Codex app 26.602 added activity insights and shareable profile cards in the Profile section. Users can review Codex usage highlights and share profile cards on consumer ChatGPT plans.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-04</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Fix with Copilot for Failing Actions</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        New 'Fix with Copilot' feature for failing GitHub Actions is now available in Copilot Pro, Pro+, and Max tiers, allowing AI-assisted debugging of workflow failures.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-04</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Visual Studio and VS Code May/June Updates</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">Release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        GitHub released Copilot updates for Visual Studio (May update) and Visual Studio Code with Copilot Chat bringing richer context to pull requests.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-03</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Design Mode Improvements with Multi-Select and Voice Input</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Cursor enhanced Design Mode with multi-select elements, voice input capabilities, and improved component styling. Users can now click multiple elements simultaneously, narrate changes by voice, and queue new instructions while agents are running.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-03</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Cursor</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">SDK Updates: Custom Tools, Auto-Review, and Nested Subagents</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Cursor SDK now supports custom tools, auto-review routing for safer headless execution, JSONL and custom stores for persistence, and nested subagents. Both TypeScript and Python SDKs received reliability and performance improvements.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-03</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">June 2026 Release Wave - Copilot Enhancements</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">Release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        GitHub released multiple Copilot updates in early June 2026, including larger context windows with configurable reasoning levels, Copilot Chat improvements for pull requests, and the general availability of Enterprise Teams.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-02</div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"End of an Era - GitHub Copilot is moving to usage-based billing on June 1, 2026.\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: Reddit (negative sentiment)</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Copilot SDK Generally Available</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">Release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        The Copilot SDK became generally available in June 2026, providing developers with programmatic access to Copilot capabilities.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-02</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Codex CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Sites Preview - Build and Deploy Websites</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Sites is now available in preview in the Codex app. Users can create, save, deploy, and inspect websites, dashboards, internal tools, web apps, and games hosted by OpenAI. Included in ChatGPT Business workspaces and available to ChatGPT Enterprise via RBAC.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-02</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Codex CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">iOS App Updates - Face ID Lock and Windows SSH Support</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">Release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        ChatGPT for iOS 1.2026.146 added optional Face ID/passcode lock for Codex, new settings screen for Queue/Steer behavior, and support for connecting to Windows machines over SSH.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-02</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Claude Code</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Opus 4.8 Released</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">Release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Claude Opus 4.8 was released as the new default model for Max/Team plans, showing improvements over Opus 4.7 in coding with notable security enhancements.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-02</div>\n                    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n                        \"Lots of people want to try Claude Opus 4.8\"\n                        <span class=\"quote-source\">Source: HN (positive sentiment)</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Codex CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Amazon Bedrock Model Provider Support</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Codex can now use supported OpenAI models available through Amazon Bedrock. Configure Amazon Bedrock as the model provider to run Codex locally with AWS-managed authentication, account controls, and billing.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-01</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Codex CLI</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Terminal Placement Controls</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">Feature</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Codex app 26.601 added Default terminal location setting. When bottom panel is enabled, users can choose whether terminal shortcuts open in bottom panel or right panel.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-06-01</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"update-item\">\n                    <div class=\"update-product\">Claude Code</div>\n                    <div class=\"update-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Week 22 Updates - v2.1.150 to v2.1.157</a>\n                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">Release</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-description\">\n                        Multiple releases during May 25-29, 2026 including improvements to rendering performance for large file writes (v2.1.169 mentioned), and ongoing iterative updates to the Claude Code tooling.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"update-meta\">2026-05-29</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights (5)</h2>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/08/microsofts-open-source-tools-were-hacked-to-steal-passwords-of-ai-developers/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft's open source tools were hacked to steal passwords of AI developers</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Microsoft shut down dozens of GitHub code repositories for Azure and AI coding tools after a security breach. Raises concerns about security in the AI development ecosystem.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                        <strong>TechCrunch</strong>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        <span>2026-06-08</span> •\n                        <span>security, microsoft, ai, github</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/openai-help-lockdown-mode/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Help: Lockdown Mode</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        OpenAI released Lockdown Mode to help prevent data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests. Simon notes this directly attacks the 'exfiltration vectors' leg of the Lethal Trifecta.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                        <strong>Simon Willison</strong>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        <span>2026-06-05</span> •\n                        <span>security, prompt-injection, llms</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/ladybird-no-public-prs/\" target=\"_blank\">Ladybird browser will no longer accept public pull requests</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Andreas Kling announced Ladybird will no longer accept public PRs because AI-generated patches no longer indicate substantial effort or good faith. Simon notes this as a sign of how AI is changing open source contribution models.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                        <strong>Simon Willison</strong>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        <span>2026-06-05</span> •\n                        <span>ai-ethics, open-source</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/ai-enthusiists-race-against-time/\" target=\"_blank\">AI enthusiasts are in a race against time, AI skeptics are in a race against entropy</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Charity Majors captures the dynamic between AI enthusiasts and skeptics: Enthusiasts are seeing discontinuous leaps in capabilities and can't afford to wait, while skeptics are seeing reliability degrade. The key insight: there is no natural feedback loop connecting these two groups.\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                        <strong>Simon Willison (quoting Charity Majors)</strong>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        <span>2026-06-04</span> •\n                        <span>ai, engineering-culture</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                    <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/3/uber-caps-ai-tools/\" target=\"_blank\">Uber Caps Usage of AI Tools Like Claude Code to Manage Costs</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                        Uber is limiting all employees to $1,500 in monthly token spending per AI coding tool (Cursor, Claude Code, etc.), after reportedly blowing their 2026 AI budget in four months. Simon calculates this as ~11% of median engineer compensation ($330k).\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-author\">\n                        <strong>Simon Willison</strong>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                        <span>2026-06-03</span> •\n                        <span>ai, cost-management, uber</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <p>Report generated by Agent Code Daily - Powered by Claude Agent SDK</p>\n        <p>Generated: 2026-06-10</p>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>"
}

